5
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
SEASON 01  #  EPISODE 10
"A Quality of Mercy"

6
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.070
<i>Previously. on </i>STAR TREK STRANGE NEW WORLDS<i>...</i>

7
00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:29.060
PIKE: <i>T'quiel Dawn.</i>

8
00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:30.390
UNA: <i>You know their names.</i>

9
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:31.790
PIKE: <i>Muliq Al Alcazar.</i>

10
00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:33.580
MAN: Get out of here!
- Aah!

11
00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:37.370
We can keep doing this. but we can also talk about it.

12
00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.500
It's classified.

13
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:41.360
UNA: <i>How do you know you can't make a different choice?</i>

14
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:42.900
Yuuto Hoshide.

15
00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:44.780
One that saves all of you?

16
00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:46.240
PIKE: Andrea Lopez.

17
00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:47.950
I accepted my fate.

18
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.680
<i>It goes beyond my own life.</i>

19
00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.280
UNA: <i>What if your fate...</i>

20
00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:55.580
is what you make it?

21
00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:58.170
PIKE: <i>Maybe that's the good in seeing my future.</i>

22
00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.130
<i>Stay the course. Save their lives.</i>

23
00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:19.980
PIKE: <i>Captain's Log. Stardate 1457.9.</i>

24
00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:22.960
<i>The</i> Enterprise <i>is on the edge of the Neutral Zone.</i>

25
00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:25.740
<i>A narrow band of space separating the Romulan Empire...</i>

26
00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:26.990
<i>from the Federation.</i>

27
00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:30.410
<i>A remnant of a treaty from 100 years ago...</i>

28
00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:33.290
<i>when a destructive war was waged between our 2 cultures.</i>

29
00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:35.790
Enterprise <i>and the</i> U.S.S. Cayuga...

30
00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.120
<i>are here to help the outposts that guard the Neutral Zone...</i>

31
00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:40.420
<i>with much-needed retrofitting and supplies.</i>

32
00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:49.220
[DOOR WHOOSHES OPEN]

33
00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:53.600
We already had spaghetti last night.

34
00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:56.730
I'm making Pasta Mama.

35
00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.940
Just add eggs. parmesan...

36
00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:05.780
lightly sauté. and it transforms from leftovers...

37
00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:08.110
into something new.
- Mmm.

38
00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:10.620
Little like what we're doing to these outposts.

39
00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:11.870
Not as tasty. though.

40
00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:17.660
Hearing rumors the Romulans are developing new weapons.

41
00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.580
Ah. the Romulans are the boogeymen.

42
00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:20.960
No one's ever seen one.

43
00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:22.630
Nobody even knows what they look like...

44
00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:25.340
and yet they get blamed for a lot of things around here.

45
00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.010
Some actually their fault.

46
00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.510
You know. I think I miss the beard.

47
00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:35.640
Yeah. I...

48
00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:38.640
It felt like it belonged to a different era of Captain.

49
00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:40.980
Thought that's what you were going for. man out of time.

50
00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:42.310
[CHUCKLES]

51
00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:47.490
How have you been holding up?

52
00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.240
Someone told me I have better places to be...

53
00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:51.620
so I'm trying to be there.

54
00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:53.620
Better places.

55
00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.330
And how's that going?

56
00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.080
You tell me.

57
00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:00.500
[CHUCKLES]

58
00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:06.090
Well. much as I love you being mysterious...

59
00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:08.170
I've got a date on the far side of the Neutral Zone.

60
00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:09.380
PIKE: Mmm.

61
00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:11.470
Anyone I know?

62
00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:12.760
Not that kind of date. actually.

63
00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:16.220
You know. I'm making osso buco next week. if you're interested.

64
00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:20.140
I mean. I'm always curious who the Chris of tomorrow is gonna be.

65
00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:21.560
Beard. no beard.

66
00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:23.690
Surprise me.

67
00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:24.860
[CHUCKLES]

68
00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:27.530
[DOOR WHOOSHES OPEN]

69
00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:30.650
AL-SALAH: <i>We are on our own out here.</i>

70
00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:33.950
How do you plan to fix our supply chain problems?

71
00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:36.790
Under the proposed retrofit directive...

72
00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:38.370
every outpost will be equipped...

73
00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:40.210
with state-of-the-art matter synthesizers...

74
00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:42.630
fueled by minerals from the asteroid itself.

75
00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.540
They will also each receive a set...

76
00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:47.300
of fully automated mining craft that can be operated remotely.

77
00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:49.970
Commander?

78
00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:51.930
How does this sound?

79
00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:55.350
Sounds like what I've been asking for for the last 5 years.

80
00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:57.390
[CHUCKLES] Well. you're welcome.

81
00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:58.390
[DOOR WHOOSHES OPEN]

82
00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:02.020
You know I'm working.

83
00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:04.400
I just wanted to meet Captain Pike.

84
00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.360
[CHUCKLES] Apologies.

85
00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:09.440
Maat has always dreamed about joining Starfleet.

86
00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:12.570
What did you say your name is?

87
00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:13.910
Maat.

88
00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:15.660
Maat Al-Salah.

89
00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:18.990
[AL-SALAH ECHOING] He has a model of the <i>Enterprise</i> back home.

90
00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:20.500
You're quite a hero of his.

91
00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:22.830
Is it true you can tell what warp you're at...

92
00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:24.750
[FADED] just by listening to the sound of the engine?

93
00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:26.460
[INDISTINCT PEOPLE SHOUTING]

94
00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:27.460
[ECHOING STOPS]

95
00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:33.430
Apologies. I... I think I need a moment.

96
00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:37.470
I'm sorry. he just gets a little excited.

97
00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:39.850
It's totally fine. I'm just feeling a little under the weather.

98
00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:42.370
Number One and Spock can answer any further questions you have.

99
00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.440
[DOOR WHOOSHES OPEN]

100
00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:56.910
[MUFFLED. INDISTINCT VOICES]

101
00:04:57.910 --> 00:04:59.330
UNA: Captain.

102
00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:01.330
[INDISTINCT PEOPLE SHOUTING]

103
00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:04.460
Chris. that boy.

104
00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:07.330
He's one of the names you mentioned.

105
00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:09.040
Yes. I wasn't expecting that.

106
00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:11.920
There's 2 cadets who don't make it. He's 1 of them.

107
00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:14.970
You don't have to face this alone.

108
00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:16.800
What are you going to do?

109
00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:17.930
I don't know.

110
00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:20.970
But I have to do something. don't I?

111
00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:22.810
[DOOR WHOOSHES OPEN]

112
00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:39.330
Computer.
- [COMPUTER CHIMES]

113
00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:41.740
Take dictation.

114
00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:47.670
Dear Maat...

115
00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:52.250
I'm gratified to see your deep interest in Starfleet...

116
00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:55.380
and I encourage you to pursue your dream...

117
00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:57.890
but there is something you should know about...

118
00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:01.050
the future?

119
00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.810
MAN: You'll figure out how to say it.

120
00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:04.390
Trust me.

121
00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:06.520
Who the hell are you?

122
00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:10.810
I thought that would've been obvious.

123
00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:15.030
I'm you.

124
00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:31.300
STAR TREK

125
00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:31.300
STRANGE

126
00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:31.300
NEW

127
00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:31.300
WＯRLDS

128
00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:31.300
SEASON 01  #  EPISODE 10
"A Quality of Mercy"

129
00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.340
PIKE: Space.

130
00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:26.540
The final frontier.

131
00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:32.710
These are the voyages of the starship Enterprise.

132
00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:35.970
Its 5-year mission...

133
00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:39.220
to explore strange new worlds...

134
00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:43.470
to seek out new life...

135
00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:46.850
and new civilizations...

136
00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:50.050
to boldly go...

137
00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:52.060
where no one has gone before.

138
00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:54.070
[ ♪ THEME MUSIC ♪ ]

139
00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:17.820
Sorry.

140
00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:21.200
It's just. this room brings back a lot of memories.

141
00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:22.900
Is this some kind of...

142
00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:23.950
Joke? No.

143
00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:26.990
How am I supposed to believe...

144
00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:28.040
That I'm really you?

145
00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:30.540
You ever gonna let me get a word in edgewise?

146
00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:33.120
I knew you were going to say that. Does that help?

147
00:08:34.170 --> 00:08:35.830
I've been doing this long enough...

148
00:08:36.170 --> 00:08:38.000
that I'm not just gonna take the word of somebody...

149
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.630
who shows up in my cabin and says he's future me.

150
00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:42.880
Mmm.

151
00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:47.640
Your 1ˢᵗ pony was named Sir Neighs-a-Lot.

152
00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:49.350
He broke his leg in a rainstorm.

153
00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:51.710
Your parents had to put him down. and you cried for a week.

154
00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:53.350
Ever tell anybody that?

155
00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:57.310
It's hard when your tragic backstory starts with...

156
00:08:57.310 --> 00:08:58.440
A silly name.

157
00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:00.070
I'm sorry.

158
00:09:00.530 --> 00:09:01.570
Look...

159
00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:04.240
I'm here because that letter you're about to write...

160
00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:05.700
is going to wreck the future.

161
00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:11.370
How. though?

162
00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:13.910
Wh...

163
00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:16.000
Why?

164
00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:19.210
2 cadets die in that accident 7 years from now.

165
00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:21.210
Maat is 1 of them.

166
00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:23.590
You're trying to figure out...

167
00:09:23.590 --> 00:09:25.760
how to save the cadets and yourself.

168
00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:27.800
And you do.

169
00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:28.800
We do.

170
00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:33.230
You write to all of them. tell them not to be there that day.

171
00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:36.650
But like so much of this time-bending stuff. there are. uh...

172
00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:39.650
unforeseen consequences.

173
00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:42.020
Well. how bad can it be...

174
00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:44.270
if I figure out a way to save all the cadets and myself?

175
00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:47.360
Hell. isn't you standing here evidence that I pull it off?

176
00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:48.700
Yes.

177
00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:51.490
And that's the problem.

178
00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:54.080
Causality is complex.

179
00:09:54.710 --> 00:09:56.960
The letter is just the 1ˢᵗ domino to fall...

180
00:09:56.960 --> 00:10:00.380
in a chain reaction of events that leads to catastrophic results.

181
00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:02.340
It alters the future...

182
00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:04.800
in ways that we never intended to change.

183
00:10:05.470 --> 00:10:08.050
You sound like one of those Klingon monks from Boreth.

184
00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:09.340
Who do you think sent me?

185
00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:12.560
They gave me something to show you.

186
00:10:17.270 --> 00:10:18.600
Is that what I think it is?

187
00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:20.810
A time crystal.

188
00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:23.860
It will show you the effects of changing your fate.

189
00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:26.400
This is serious.

190
00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:29.740
This is end-of-the-world stuff.

191
00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:33.580
I know that you would never...

192
00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:36.620
put your own fate before the fate of the galaxy.

193
00:10:39.210 --> 00:10:40.880
And that's how I convinced the Klingons...

194
00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:42.210
to let me show you instead.

195
00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:45.460
Instead of what?

196
00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:48.130
You know the Klingons.

197
00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:51.510
Nothing they wouldn't rather solve with a bat'leth.

198
00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:21.540
I...

199
00:11:23.840 --> 00:11:25.210
Captain?

200
00:11:25.210 --> 00:11:26.590
Uh. sorry.

201
00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:28.880
What was I saying?

202
00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:31.430
Um. that since the age of wooden ships...

203
00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:35.390
all shipmasters have had a happy privilege of...

204
00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:36.970
Right.

205
00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:41.560
I assume I was... I was talking about weddings?

206
00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:42.560
Yeah?

207
00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:45.940
Which we get to perform. as Captains...

208
00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:48.530
on ships.

209
00:11:48.530 --> 00:11:50.150
So...

210
00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:51.410
we take you...

211
00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:55.870
and you. uh...

212
00:11:56.540 --> 00:11:57.790
and you...

213
00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:00.660
both want to get married.

214
00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:01.750
So...
- [ALARM BLARING]

215
00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:03.040
COMPUTER: <i>All decks. red alert.</i>

216
00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:05.210
<i>Repeat. all decks. red alert.</i>

217
00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:07.840
Thank God.

218
00:12:09.550 --> 00:12:11.220
SPOCK: <i>Number One to Captain Pike.</i>

219
00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:14.010
<i>Outpost 4 reports they are under attack...</i>

220
00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:16.390
<i>by a space vessel. identity unknown.</i>

221
00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:19.270
Copy. Mr. Spock.

222
00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:21.060
On my way.

223
00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:24.150
[BOATSWAIN'S WHISTLE BLOWS]

224
00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:30.070
What's the situation. Mr. Spock?

225
00:12:30.570 --> 00:12:32.700
Lieutenant Uhura can brief you.

226
00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:41.460
Outpost 4 reported under attack. sir.

227
00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:43.580
Then message terminates.

228
00:12:55.760 --> 00:12:57.100
Any word from 2 or 3?

229
00:12:58.640 --> 00:13:00.430
2 has not responded to our hails...

230
00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:01.930
and 3 has also gone silent.

231
00:13:01.930 --> 00:13:03.270
How far out are we. Erica?

232
00:13:03.270 --> 00:13:05.600
8 minutes from Outpost 4 at this velocity. sir.

233
00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:08.060
Did Outpost 4 say anything else about the attacking vessel?

234
00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:09.770
No identification. sir.

235
00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:12.240
ORTEGAS: I'm guessing it's the same attackers. sir.

236
00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:14.110
The Romulans.

237
00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:22.910
Let's not make guesses just yet.

238
00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:25.460
I'd like to avoid a war if I can.

239
00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:28.960
Maintain course. Alert me when we're 2 minutes out.

240
00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:31.160
Mr. Spock. could you join me in the Ready Room. please?

241
00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:33.050
2266.

242
00:13:34.510 --> 00:13:35.930
7 years into the future.

243
00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:38.760
I do not understand.

244
00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:40.970
Is this one of your human jokes?

245
00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:42.470
I'm serious. Spock. This is...

246
00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:45.940
Well. it's time crystal stuff.

247
00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:47.440
Approaching this logically...

248
00:13:47.850 --> 00:13:50.020
time travel seems a less likely solution...

249
00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:52.150
than that you are compromised mentally.

250
00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:53.860
And as your 1ˢᵗ Officer...

251
00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:57.030
in these circumstances. it is my job to assume command.

252
00:13:57.030 --> 00:13:59.780
I agree. if I was mentally compromised.

253
00:13:59.780 --> 00:14:01.030
But I am not.

254
00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:03.940
So. what's the logical solution?

255
00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:06.460
Perhaps the Doctor could do a full scan.

256
00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:07.790
Why don't we try a mind-meld?

257
00:14:08.210 --> 00:14:09.880
That way you'll know if I'm lying or not.

258
00:14:21.470 --> 00:14:23.930
My mind to your mind.

259
00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:27.310
My thoughts to your thoughts.

260
00:14:35.190 --> 00:14:37.200
[SCREAMING]

261
00:14:39.030 --> 00:14:40.160
SPOCK: You...

262
00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:42.620
carry the weight of a terrible future. Chris.

263
00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:46.330
The accident in question was 6 months ago.

264
00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:51.000
In this timeline...

265
00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.880
there were no cadets at the reactor incident to save.

266
00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:55.590
No one was even hurt.

267
00:14:55.590 --> 00:14:56.920
I need your help. Spock.

268
00:14:57.550 --> 00:15:00.220
I was sent forward to this moment in time for a reason.

269
00:15:00.470 --> 00:15:01.720
We have to figure out why.

270
00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:03.720
I would posit that in this present...

271
00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:05.510
you were never injured in the training accident...

272
00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:07.890
thus. you remained Captain of the <i>Enterprise</i>...

273
00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:09.730
putting you in charge at a crucial moment...

274
00:15:09.730 --> 00:15:10.900
in the ship's existence.

275
00:15:10.900 --> 00:15:13.860
A moment where the whole future hangs in the balance.

276
00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:15.360
SPOCK: All we can surmise...

277
00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:17.070
is that. in the Prime future...

278
00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:20.740
some other Captain of the <i>Enterprise</i> must have commanded it differently.

279
00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:23.370
Thus. it is imperative you do not change...

280
00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:25.200
what you would normally do on the ship.

281
00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:27.080
I thought we were trying to avoid a terrible future.

282
00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:30.080
We are trying to discover why this future is...

283
00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:33.040
in the estimation of your older self. worse.

284
00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:35.250
So. the only way to discover the terrible future...

285
00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:38.050
is to live it.

286
00:15:41.010 --> 00:15:43.010
[ENGINE WHIRRING]

287
00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:51.020
ORTEGAS: Enterprise <i>is in position and holding. sir.</i>

288
00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:52.600
Just out of weapons range.

289
00:15:53.940 --> 00:15:55.650
Detecting a fair amount of debris...

290
00:15:55.650 --> 00:15:57.150
but no sign of any attacking ship.

291
00:15:57.150 --> 00:15:58.360
Let's triple check.

292
00:15:58.360 --> 00:16:00.950
Nyota. see if there are any other Federation ships in the vicinity...

293
00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:02.030
in case we need backup.

294
00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:04.070
The <i>Farragut</i> is closest.

295
00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:05.330
A couple hours away.

296
00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:09.580
That's La'An's ship. sir.

297
00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:12.960
Yes. I'd forgotten.

298
00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:17.710
Sir. we're being hailed.

299
00:16:17.710 --> 00:16:19.670
It's the outpost. Audio only.

300
00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:23.130
AL-SALAH: Enterprise. <i>can you read me?</i>

301
00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:25.220
<i>This is Commander Hansen Al-Salah.</i>

302
00:16:26.350 --> 00:16:27.970
This is Pike. What's your status?

303
00:16:27.970 --> 00:16:30.350
<i>Outposts 2. 3. & 8 are gone.</i>

304
00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:33.560
<i>Unknown weapon. Completely destroyed.</i>

305
00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:35.850
<i>We had our deflector shields on maximum.</i>

306
00:16:35.860 --> 00:16:37.980
<i>Hit by enormous power.</i>

307
00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:40.320
<i>1ˢᵗ attack blew through our shields.</i>

308
00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:43.490
<i>If they hit us again with our deflectors gone...</i>

309
00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:45.320
<i>Do you read me.</i> Enterprise?

310
00:16:45.320 --> 00:16:47.830
What hit you. Commander? What vessel? Can you identify?

311
00:16:47.830 --> 00:16:50.370
<i>Negative. It all happened so fast.</i>

312
00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:53.290
<i>And it seems to have disappeared somehow.</i>

313
00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:54.670
<i>Switching to visual.</i>

314
00:16:55.830 --> 00:16:58.500
Enterprise. <i>can you see?</i>

315
00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:00.880
<i>My command post here.</i>

316
00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:03.670
<i>We're a mile deep. on an asteroid...</i>

317
00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:06.220
[ALARM BLARING]
- almost solid iron...

318
00:17:06.220 --> 00:17:08.640
and even through our deflectors. it did this.

319
00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:10.930
<i>Can you see?</i>
- We see. Hansen.

320
00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:12.980
Was your son with you?

321
00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:14.770
No. thank God.

322
00:17:17.060 --> 00:17:18.690
What can you tell us about the attacker?

323
00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:19.770
No identity.

324
00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:21.400
Only a glimpse of it.

325
00:17:22.490 --> 00:17:24.490
Then it fired something at us.

326
00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:26.660
<i>High-energy plasma.</i>

327
00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:28.870
<i>Fantastic power.</i>

328
00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:33.080
Vessel seems to have disappeared...

329
00:17:33.080 --> 00:17:34.870
but it is out there somewhere.

330
00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:37.880
[PANTING] Enterprise...

331
00:17:37.880 --> 00:17:40.000
there's something on our sensors. moving fast.

332
00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:41.800
Send us your signal.
<i>- Switching.</i>

333
00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:45.760
Enterprise. <i>can you see in the center of my screen?</i>

334
00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:47.840
Phasers?
- Still out of range. sir.

335
00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:49.600
We're out of range. Commander. Do you have weapons?

336
00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:50.850
<i>Negative. Phasers gone.</i>

337
00:17:50.850 --> 00:17:52.100
<i>Weapon crew are all dead.</i>

338
00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:53.430
Hail them. Warn that ship off.

339
00:17:53.430 --> 00:17:55.640
I'm trying. They're not acknowledging us.

340
00:18:01.070 --> 00:18:02.400
Aah!

341
00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:27.760
Interesting how they became visible for just a moment.

342
00:18:27.760 --> 00:18:29.510
Perhaps necessary to use weapons.

343
00:18:29.510 --> 00:18:33.060
Sir. We have to find a way to engage them.

344
00:18:33.060 --> 00:18:34.810
We need something to follow. Lieutenant.

345
00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:35.930
We have no visuals.

346
00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:38.390
Analyzing their movement patterns now.

347
00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:39.480
Give me a moment.

348
00:18:43.610 --> 00:18:45.860
Sir? Incoming warp signature.

349
00:18:46.440 --> 00:18:48.860
We're being hailed.
- [SYSTEM CHIMING]

350
00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:50.780
It's one of ours. The <i>Farragut.</i>

351
00:18:50.780 --> 00:18:52.030
La'An's ship?

352
00:18:52.620 --> 00:18:54.540
Who's hailing us?
- UHURA: Their Captain.

353
00:18:54.870 --> 00:18:56.000
James Kirk.

354
00:18:57.830 --> 00:18:58.830
Sam's brother?

355
00:19:00.420 --> 00:19:02.380
Uh... I mean. uh...

356
00:19:03.130 --> 00:19:04.460
On screen.

357
00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:08.090
<i>Enterprise.</i> this is Captain James T. Kirk...

358
00:19:08.090 --> 00:19:10.510
of the <i>U.S.S. Farragut.</i> offering assistance.

359
00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:16.010
Christopher Pike. Good to see you. Captain.

360
00:19:16.020 --> 00:19:18.390
<i>We received Outpost 4's distress signal...</i>

361
00:19:18.390 --> 00:19:20.980
<i>and pushed Warp 9 for as long as we safely could.</i>

362
00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:23.190
<i>Do we know who did this?</i>
- We have a pretty good idea.

363
00:19:23.190 --> 00:19:24.900
We're trying to determine conclusively.

364
00:19:25.940 --> 00:19:27.240
I may have a lead. sir.

365
00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:30.650
The ship in question appears to have a kind of cloaking device.

366
00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:32.950
But they still have a detectable gravitational presence.

367
00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:35.240
So. can we track it. Commander...

368
00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:36.330
Spock.

369
00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:37.830
Theoretically. yes.

370
00:19:37.830 --> 00:19:40.000
By detecting the microlensing of background stars...

371
00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:41.710
we can determine an approximate location.

372
00:19:41.710 --> 00:19:43.170
Impressive. Mr. Spock.

373
00:19:43.170 --> 00:19:44.500
Where's the intruder now?

374
00:19:46.590 --> 00:19:49.210
He has changed heading. At a very leisurely maneuver.

375
00:19:49.220 --> 00:19:51.220
They may not be aware of us.
- How can that be true?

376
00:19:51.220 --> 00:19:53.050
They had to decloak to fire.

377
00:19:53.050 --> 00:19:54.890
Their device may work both ways.

378
00:19:54.890 --> 00:19:56.510
It makes them invisible to our sensors...

379
00:19:56.510 --> 00:19:58.770
but requires a massive amount of energy.

380
00:19:58.770 --> 00:20:00.020
<i>They are likely flying blind...</i>

381
00:20:00.020 --> 00:20:01.690
<i>without enough power to run their scanners.</i>

382
00:20:01.690 --> 00:20:04.650
So. we can't see them. but they can't see us.

383
00:20:07.230 --> 00:20:08.440
[BEEPING]

384
00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:12.530
His heading is now 1-1-1. mark 1-4.

385
00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:14.740
The exact heading a Romulan vessel would take...

386
00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:16.370
toward the Neutral Zone and home.

387
00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:18.700
Sir. it's the Romulans.

388
00:20:19.370 --> 00:20:20.750
We have to take them out.

389
00:20:20.750 --> 00:20:23.210
We can't enter the Neutral Zone. Starfleet is clear on this.

390
00:20:23.210 --> 00:20:24.830
We do. that's considered an act of war.

391
00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:26.500
They destroyed 3 of our outposts.

392
00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:27.880
That's not an act of war?

393
00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:29.550
We attack the Romulans without authorization...

394
00:20:29.550 --> 00:20:31.220
the Federation will consider us expendable.

395
00:20:31.220 --> 00:20:32.680
KIRK: <i>We do have another option.</i>

396
00:20:33.050 --> 00:20:34.680
<i>We can shadow the ship.</i>

397
00:20:34.680 --> 00:20:37.220
Follow a parallel course. to buy us some time.

398
00:20:37.220 --> 00:20:39.520
Not an intercept course. sir?
<i>- No.</i>

399
00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:42.270
The Captain is right. That would be a declaration of war.

400
00:20:42.270 --> 00:20:43.850
<i>But if</i> Enterprise <i>and</i> Farragut...

401
00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:46.400
<i>match course and speed with the enemy ship. exactly...</i>

402
00:20:46.400 --> 00:20:47.400
<i>move for move...</i>

403
00:20:47.690 --> 00:20:49.400
they might think we're just a reflection.

404
00:20:49.400 --> 00:20:50.780
Echoes on their sensors.

405
00:20:51.030 --> 00:20:52.320
<i>That way we won't lose them...</i>

406
00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:54.000
<i>while we wait to hear back from Starfleet.</i>

407
00:20:54.820 --> 00:20:56.320
Let's start shadowing them.

408
00:20:57.450 --> 00:20:59.370
Uhura. send a message to Starfleet.

409
00:20:59.370 --> 00:21:01.080
Ask for permission to engage the Romulans.

410
00:21:01.750 --> 00:21:03.410
Captain Kirk. we'll be talking.

411
00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:05.460
I look forward to it. Kirk out.

412
00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:11.170
Get Sam Kirk up here. ASAP.

413
00:21:12.130 --> 00:21:14.590
SAM: Am I off the record here. sir?

414
00:21:16.430 --> 00:21:18.430
Jim was always at the top of his class.

415
00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:21.980
He's smart and highly skilled. obviously...

416
00:21:22.600 --> 00:21:26.060
but he's not above relying on charm or even luck.

417
00:21:26.860 --> 00:21:28.310
Sounds like a wild card.

418
00:21:28.310 --> 00:21:29.610
A whole deck of 'em.

419
00:21:30.780 --> 00:21:33.110
He doesn't like to take the path everyone else does.

420
00:21:33.650 --> 00:21:35.360
And he doesn't like to lose.

421
00:21:39.620 --> 00:21:42.790
Should we be worried that he's going to start a war?

422
00:21:45.830 --> 00:21:48.960
Look. I'm not gonna say that Jim isn't a pain in the ass.

423
00:21:49.380 --> 00:21:51.550
He is. He's a huge pain in the ass.

424
00:21:52.510 --> 00:21:53.880
But the truth is...

425
00:21:53.880 --> 00:21:56.510
he's as fine a Captain as Starfleet has.

426
00:21:57.640 --> 00:21:58.840
Okay. Good to know.

427
00:21:58.850 --> 00:22:01.310
Like I said. he does like to bend the rules sometimes.

428
00:22:02.220 --> 00:22:04.350
No. more like all the time.

429
00:22:04.730 --> 00:22:05.810
[COMMS CHIMING]

430
00:22:05.810 --> 00:22:07.640
SPOCK: <i>Captain. can you come to the bridge?</i>

431
00:22:07.650 --> 00:22:09.310
<i>There is something you should see.</i>

432
00:22:10.060 --> 00:22:11.320
UHURA: There's a comet ahead...

433
00:22:11.320 --> 00:22:14.650
and its trail is reflecting a signal on an unused EM frequency.

434
00:22:14.650 --> 00:22:17.410
It is encoded. Mr. Spock is trying to decipher.

435
00:22:17.660 --> 00:22:19.660
But we think it might be from the enemy ship.

436
00:22:20.580 --> 00:22:23.330
They cut off transmission. but we managed to make a copy.

437
00:22:24.830 --> 00:22:26.500
I think it's the feed from their bridge. sir.

438
00:22:26.500 --> 00:22:29.170
So. we're finally going to see what the Romulans look like.

439
00:22:30.540 --> 00:22:32.380
Put it on screen. please. Mr. Spock.

440
00:23:05.620 --> 00:23:06.960
[SOFT WARBLING]

441
00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:12.540
PIKE: Captain Kirk...

442
00:23:12.540 --> 00:23:14.090
welcome aboard the <i>Enterprise.</i>

443
00:23:14.090 --> 00:23:15.380
Thanks. Captain Pike.

444
00:23:15.800 --> 00:23:16.880
Sam.

445
00:23:20.840 --> 00:23:22.140
Quite the ship you got here.

446
00:23:22.140 --> 00:23:23.220
He's jealous.

447
00:23:23.220 --> 00:23:24.430
[KIRK CHUCKLING]

448
00:23:27.680 --> 00:23:29.230
Well. we're not gonna get out of this problem...

449
00:23:29.230 --> 00:23:30.520
by not talking about it.

450
00:23:31.560 --> 00:23:32.610
Agreed.

451
00:23:32.860 --> 00:23:35.060
I'd like to hear what Mr. Spock has to say for himself.

452
00:23:36.070 --> 00:23:37.280
I assure you. Lieutenant...

453
00:23:37.280 --> 00:23:39.570
the similarities between Vulcans and Romulans...

454
00:23:39.570 --> 00:23:40.990
came as a surprise to me.

455
00:23:40.990 --> 00:23:42.410
Perhaps even more so than you.

456
00:23:42.410 --> 00:23:43.830
It does seem suspicious.

457
00:23:44.240 --> 00:23:45.740
Not the similarity itself...

458
00:23:45.740 --> 00:23:47.660
but the fact that we should discover it right now.

459
00:23:47.660 --> 00:23:48.870
What are you suggesting?

460
00:23:48.870 --> 00:23:50.710
Well. it's no secret that the Vulcans and the humans...

461
00:23:50.710 --> 00:23:51.920
are in alliance.

462
00:23:51.920 --> 00:23:54.580
Perhaps the Romulans allowed us to see that transmission...

463
00:23:54.590 --> 00:23:57.050
in hopes that it would sow discord among us.

464
00:23:57.050 --> 00:24:00.170
Even if we ignore the pointy-eared elephant in the room...

465
00:24:00.170 --> 00:24:02.590
we have another problem to worry about.

466
00:24:02.590 --> 00:24:04.010
We're going to lose our prey.

467
00:24:04.010 --> 00:24:05.390
MITCHELL: The Romulans are on a bearing...

468
00:24:05.390 --> 00:24:07.390
to return to the Neutral Zone in an hour.

469
00:24:07.390 --> 00:24:08.850
KIRK: I don't think we can wait.

470
00:24:08.850 --> 00:24:10.310
We have to make a choice here.

471
00:24:10.310 --> 00:24:11.980
SPOCK: Say we do make that choice.

472
00:24:11.980 --> 00:24:14.900
Their plasma weapon can still slice through our shields.

473
00:24:14.900 --> 00:24:16.940
That. in conjunction with their cloaking device...

474
00:24:16.940 --> 00:24:18.440
gives them a tactical advantage.

475
00:24:18.440 --> 00:24:20.440
Even against our ships working in tandem.

476
00:24:20.450 --> 00:24:22.320
M'BENGA: Working in tandem for what?

477
00:24:22.320 --> 00:24:23.610
To destroy them?

478
00:24:25.120 --> 00:24:26.990
Say we're lucky enough to do that.

479
00:24:26.990 --> 00:24:31.000
Isn't that. technically. an act of war?

480
00:24:31.460 --> 00:24:33.040
ORTEGAS: I hate to say it. Doc...

481
00:24:33.040 --> 00:24:34.750
but they started it.

482
00:24:34.750 --> 00:24:36.040
This isn't a schoolyard.

483
00:24:36.590 --> 00:24:38.550
Billions of lives are at stake here.

484
00:24:38.550 --> 00:24:41.630
Which is why I want to hear everyone's opinion...

485
00:24:41.630 --> 00:24:43.220
before we take any action.

486
00:24:44.970 --> 00:24:47.310
I vote against war.
- ORTEGAS: So do I.

487
00:24:48.100 --> 00:24:50.730
I just think that means killing Romulans.

488
00:24:53.560 --> 00:24:55.650
Captain. your thoughts?

489
00:24:58.480 --> 00:25:00.690
What happens when they return to Romulus...

490
00:25:00.690 --> 00:25:01.940
and tell their leaders...

491
00:25:01.940 --> 00:25:03.740
that the Federation won't even fight back?

492
00:25:04.660 --> 00:25:06.490
I'm starting to lean toward attack.

493
00:25:06.490 --> 00:25:09.990
If we allow them to destroy our outposts with no repercussions...

494
00:25:09.990 --> 00:25:11.330
we run the risk of war.

495
00:25:11.660 --> 00:25:13.500
Have to believe there's another way forward.

496
00:25:13.500 --> 00:25:15.040
I think we should attack.

497
00:25:16.830 --> 00:25:17.960
Mr. Spock?

498
00:25:17.960 --> 00:25:20.750
If the Romulans are an offshoot of my Vulcan blood...

499
00:25:20.760 --> 00:25:22.010
which I believe...

500
00:25:22.010 --> 00:25:24.010
then attack is indeed the only option.

501
00:25:24.510 --> 00:25:27.550
Vulcan. like Earth. had its aggressive colonizing period.

502
00:25:27.550 --> 00:25:29.390
Savage. even by human standards.

503
00:25:30.010 --> 00:25:32.180
If the Romulans retain this martial philosophy...

504
00:25:33.020 --> 00:25:35.190
then weakness is something we dare not show.

505
00:25:36.350 --> 00:25:39.610
Well. if Spock and I can agree...

506
00:25:39.610 --> 00:25:41.070
then there's hope for all of us.

507
00:25:41.070 --> 00:25:42.440
We don't all agree.

508
00:25:45.150 --> 00:25:48.370
KIRK: Hold a moment. Captain Pike. that comet we're approaching...

509
00:25:48.370 --> 00:25:50.870
might just be the alternative that you've been looking for.

510
00:25:50.870 --> 00:25:53.450
Mr. Spock. can you put up the trajectory on screen. please?

511
00:25:55.040 --> 00:25:57.540
Currently. the Romulan ship is headed for the comet's tail.

512
00:25:57.540 --> 00:25:59.080
Now. I know that they're invisible...

513
00:25:59.090 --> 00:26:01.170
and we can't lock on to their exact position.

514
00:26:01.170 --> 00:26:03.510
But the second they go through that...

515
00:26:03.510 --> 00:26:05.760
particle distortion will reveal their location.

516
00:26:05.760 --> 00:26:08.090
And we'll be flanking them on either side.

517
00:26:08.090 --> 00:26:10.390
KIRK: They'll be penned in. and we'll be able to get weapons locked.

518
00:26:10.390 --> 00:26:11.810
Good plan. Captain.

519
00:26:14.230 --> 00:26:17.600
<i>Captain's Personal Log. Stardate 1709.2.</i>

520
00:26:17.600 --> 00:26:20.900
<i>Per Captain Kirk's plan. we are mounting a pincer move.</i>

521
00:26:20.900 --> 00:26:25.150
<i>Our 2 ships will slowly drift closer as the Romulans remain unaware.</i>

522
00:26:25.150 --> 00:26:26.820
<i>When they pass through the comet's tail...</i>

523
00:26:26.820 --> 00:26:28.610
<i>giving us their exact location...</i>

524
00:26:28.610 --> 00:26:30.200
<i>we will be in weapons range.</i>

525
00:26:31.240 --> 00:26:33.080
<i>Kirk. however. has agreed to my plan...</i>

526
00:26:33.080 --> 00:26:35.700
<i>to neutralize. not destroy. the bird-of-prey...</i>

527
00:26:35.710 --> 00:26:37.750
<i>leaving open the possibility of dialogue.</i>

528
00:26:38.420 --> 00:26:40.920
<i>And yet I remain concerned...</i>

529
00:26:40.920 --> 00:26:44.210
<i>this brash. young Starfleet Captain follows his own rules.</i>

530
00:26:45.340 --> 00:26:46.720
<i>I can't help but wonder...</i>

531
00:26:46.720 --> 00:26:48.510
<i>is Kirk the reason I was sent here?</i>

532
00:26:49.010 --> 00:26:51.050
<i>If I wasn't here to stop him...</i>

533
00:26:51.050 --> 00:26:52.890
<i>would we be led into a war?</i>

534
00:26:52.890 --> 00:26:55.430
Ortegas. maintain present course. but be ready.

535
00:26:55.430 --> 00:26:58.600
I'll keep my foot over the gas. just in case.

536
00:27:00.480 --> 00:27:03.270
SPOCK: <i>Still tracking the gravitational presence of the Romulans.</i>

537
00:27:04.070 --> 00:27:05.690
<i>Their trajectory remains unchanged.</i>

538
00:27:06.190 --> 00:27:07.440
Holding position.

539
00:27:07.450 --> 00:27:08.900
Let us know when you see them. <i>Enterprise.</i>

540
00:27:08.910 --> 00:27:10.780
We're passing through the tail.

541
00:27:10.780 --> 00:27:12.240
Any second now.

542
00:27:22.170 --> 00:27:23.790
[INDISTINCT CHATTER OVER COMMS]

543
00:27:27.090 --> 00:27:28.470
Something isn't right.

544
00:27:28.470 --> 00:27:30.550
The Captain is correct. We should have seen them by now.

545
00:27:30.550 --> 00:27:32.220
<i>Enterprise.</i> I don't like this.

546
00:27:32.220 --> 00:27:33.300
[BEEPING]

547
00:27:33.300 --> 00:27:35.180
SPOCK: Reading gravitational signature again.

548
00:27:35.180 --> 00:27:36.510
It's behind the <i>Farragut.</i>

549
00:27:36.520 --> 00:27:38.560
Kirk. get out of there!
- Red Alert!

550
00:27:38.560 --> 00:27:41.480
Red Alert. Erica. close that distance as fast as you can.

551
00:27:41.480 --> 00:27:43.150
Attack pattern Tiberius 4.

552
00:27:51.490 --> 00:27:52.700
<i>Get behind them.</i>

553
00:27:55.370 --> 00:27:57.370
[ALARM BEEPING]

554
00:27:59.620 --> 00:28:00.790
Fire!

555
00:28:02.460 --> 00:28:03.830
[GRUNTING]

556
00:28:15.350 --> 00:28:17.350
[ALARMS BLARING]

557
00:28:21.020 --> 00:28:22.350
Fire phasers. Captain.

558
00:28:22.350 --> 00:28:24.400
We're out of range. We're just as likely to hit you as them.

559
00:28:24.400 --> 00:28:25.860
Maybe you'll draw their fire.

560
00:28:25.860 --> 00:28:27.360
Mitchell. full phasers now.

561
00:28:33.700 --> 00:28:35.700
Holy... We actually clipped them.

562
00:28:35.700 --> 00:28:36.780
Nice shooting. Jenna.

563
00:28:36.780 --> 00:28:38.580
Nyota. hail them. I want them focused on us.

564
00:28:38.580 --> 00:28:39.910
Hailing. sir.

565
00:28:40.160 --> 00:28:41.370
Keep firing.

566
00:28:51.720 --> 00:28:53.520
MITCHELL: They're firing their plasma weapon.

567
00:28:53.840 --> 00:28:55.300
Brace for impact!

568
00:28:58.970 --> 00:29:00.310
[GRUNTING]

569
00:29:02.520 --> 00:29:04.440
Damage to Decks 6. 7 & 9.

570
00:29:04.440 --> 00:29:05.810
And weapon control is down.

571
00:29:05.810 --> 00:29:07.810
That should have destroyed us. How are we still standing?

572
00:29:07.820 --> 00:29:09.150
SPOCK: They were shooting at a distance.

573
00:29:09.150 --> 00:29:10.230
Perhaps their plasma weapon...

574
00:29:10.230 --> 00:29:11.900
is less effective when fired long range.

575
00:29:11.900 --> 00:29:12.990
Status of the <i>Farragut?</i>

576
00:29:14.360 --> 00:29:16.910
Critical. They will lose life support inside of 5 minutes.

577
00:29:16.910 --> 00:29:18.580
I can get us there in 30 seconds.

578
00:29:18.580 --> 00:29:20.580
Pike to Transporter. Get the pads warmed up. Chief.

579
00:29:20.580 --> 00:29:22.140
We're about to test their upper limits.

580
00:29:23.160 --> 00:29:24.670
[SOFT WARBLING]

581
00:29:25.080 --> 00:29:27.080
Clear the pads. There's 1 more group behind us.

582
00:29:28.880 --> 00:29:31.170
[SIGHS] Am I glad to see you.

583
00:29:33.010 --> 00:29:34.180
Oh. um...

584
00:29:35.010 --> 00:29:37.140
I didn't know you were a hugger. Lieutenant.

585
00:29:38.010 --> 00:29:39.010
Oh. Commander.

586
00:29:40.470 --> 00:29:42.060
Or have you forgotten?

587
00:29:42.060 --> 00:29:43.520
I... Of course I haven't.

588
00:29:43.520 --> 00:29:44.730
Speaking of...

589
00:29:44.980 --> 00:29:46.540
when's the last time you talked to Una?

590
00:29:48.360 --> 00:29:50.270
Well. I... I can't talk to her.

591
00:29:50.780 --> 00:29:51.980
No one can. It...

592
00:29:53.650 --> 00:29:54.990
She's not allowed contact.

593
00:29:55.780 --> 00:29:57.070
Of course.

594
00:29:57.070 --> 00:29:58.950
[SOFT WARBLING]

595
00:29:58.950 --> 00:30:00.030
KIRK: Captain Pike.

596
00:30:00.030 --> 00:30:01.290
We need to talk. Now.

597
00:30:07.670 --> 00:30:08.750
You flinched.

598
00:30:10.090 --> 00:30:12.210
You deliberated. and we lost.

599
00:30:12.210 --> 00:30:14.130
We fired. Captain. And we were fired upon.

600
00:30:14.130 --> 00:30:15.220
That's why you're still here.

601
00:30:15.220 --> 00:30:16.300
From the start...

602
00:30:16.300 --> 00:30:18.090
you wanted to cripple them. not take them out.

603
00:30:18.090 --> 00:30:19.720
We may have different points of view...

604
00:30:20.720 --> 00:30:23.720
but do not question my combat readiness. Captain.

605
00:30:23.720 --> 00:30:26.100
I'm saying caution means...

606
00:30:26.100 --> 00:30:28.810
you're not going to put everything you have into the punch.

607
00:30:28.810 --> 00:30:30.440
And that's a good way to lose...

608
00:30:30.440 --> 00:30:33.440
because your enemy will see that and act accordingly.

609
00:30:33.440 --> 00:30:35.240
All this because of a second's delay?

610
00:30:35.240 --> 00:30:37.320
Tell me I'm wrong. Captain...

611
00:30:38.240 --> 00:30:39.570
and I will back down.

612
00:30:40.320 --> 00:30:42.620
If you're saying you're more willing to take risks than I am...

613
00:30:42.620 --> 00:30:43.740
I don't disagree.

614
00:30:43.740 --> 00:30:46.000
And let me remind you that you're saying that on my ship...

615
00:30:46.000 --> 00:30:47.290
after yours has been destroyed.

616
00:30:51.170 --> 00:30:52.500
Fair.

617
00:30:52.500 --> 00:30:55.420
I'm just saying. I underestimated him.

618
00:30:55.420 --> 00:30:57.010
I'm not going to do it again.

619
00:30:57.010 --> 00:30:58.130
[COMMS CHIMING]

620
00:30:58.130 --> 00:30:59.840
SPOCK: <i>Captains Pike and Kirk to the bridge.</i>

621
00:30:59.840 --> 00:31:01.560
<i>There is something you'll both want to see.</i>

622
00:31:03.390 --> 00:31:04.720
[DOOR WHOOSHES OPEN]

623
00:31:07.350 --> 00:31:09.810
Before they cloaked. I was able to scan the bird-of-prey.

624
00:31:09.810 --> 00:31:11.480
They are trailing trilithium fragments.

625
00:31:11.480 --> 00:31:13.190
Their power supply is damaged.

626
00:31:13.190 --> 00:31:15.320
I do not believe they have enough to make it back to Romulus.

627
00:31:15.320 --> 00:31:16.990
Do we know their position?
- SPOCK: Yes.

628
00:31:16.990 --> 00:31:18.360
On a heading for the Neutral Zone.

629
00:31:18.360 --> 00:31:19.450
We could overtake them.

630
00:31:19.450 --> 00:31:20.780
What's the status of our weapons?

631
00:31:20.780 --> 00:31:22.530
Our offensive capabilities are limited.

632
00:31:22.530 --> 00:31:23.780
Phasers are down.

633
00:31:23.780 --> 00:31:25.910
And torpedo launch tubes sustained damage in the attack.

634
00:31:25.910 --> 00:31:27.290
But the Romulans don't know that.

635
00:31:27.290 --> 00:31:29.410
They will if we pull up on their 6 and can't fire.

636
00:31:29.420 --> 00:31:31.710
Lieutenant Uhura. open a channel to the Romulan ship.

637
00:31:32.590 --> 00:31:35.460
Sir? They haven't responded to any of our hails before.

638
00:31:35.460 --> 00:31:37.260
I know. Open a channel.

639
00:31:37.260 --> 00:31:38.970
We're going to send them a message.

640
00:31:39.550 --> 00:31:40.760
What are you doing?

641
00:31:43.050 --> 00:31:44.220
Taking a risk.

642
00:31:46.560 --> 00:31:48.230
[COMM CHANNEL CHIMES]

643
00:31:48.850 --> 00:31:51.170
This is Captain Christopher Pike of the <i>U.S.S. Enterprise.</i>

644
00:31:52.350 --> 00:31:54.730
Our 2 cultures have been at war for 100 years.

645
00:31:55.770 --> 00:31:57.490
Long enough that we don't even question it.

646
00:31:58.110 --> 00:31:59.950
But I believe we can make another choice.

647
00:32:00.990 --> 00:32:02.070
Right now.

648
00:32:02.410 --> 00:32:05.160
I'm offering you a temporary cease-fire...

649
00:32:05.160 --> 00:32:06.490
so that we can talk.

650
00:32:07.200 --> 00:32:09.790
For the 1ˢᵗ time in 100 years.

651
00:32:18.880 --> 00:32:21.590
Okay. That was unexpected.

652
00:32:21.590 --> 00:32:24.340
They want to destroy us. but they also want to get home.

653
00:32:24.350 --> 00:32:27.260
Knowing what your opponent wants is key to a successful negotiation.

654
00:32:27.260 --> 00:32:29.850
That's assuming they can be negotiated with.

655
00:32:30.180 --> 00:32:32.100
[SYSTEM CHIMING]

656
00:32:32.100 --> 00:32:34.850
Captain Pike. the Romulans are calling.

657
00:32:34.860 --> 00:32:36.260
Looks like we're about to find out.

658
00:32:37.190 --> 00:32:38.610
On screen. please. Nyota.

659
00:32:43.280 --> 00:32:44.570
<i>Captain Pike...</i>

660
00:32:45.200 --> 00:32:47.280
it is good to make your acquaintance.

661
00:32:56.630 --> 00:32:57.920
Commander.

662
00:32:58.750 --> 00:33:01.170
I know your ships attacked our outposts...

663
00:33:01.170 --> 00:33:02.510
on the edge of the Neutral Zone.

664
00:33:03.050 --> 00:33:04.180
<i>But I also know...</i>

665
00:33:04.180 --> 00:33:06.470
<i>that our 2 cultures have been at war for generations...</i>

666
00:33:06.470 --> 00:33:08.140
without ever having been face-to-face.

667
00:33:08.140 --> 00:33:10.970
I don't know why your ancestors attacked Earth...

668
00:33:10.980 --> 00:33:13.560
or what my ancestors did in retaliation.

669
00:33:13.560 --> 00:33:15.230
I only know that we're paying a bill...

670
00:33:15.230 --> 00:33:17.270
that was written long before you and I were ever born.

671
00:33:17.270 --> 00:33:19.400
Perhaps it's time we reconsider the cost.

672
00:33:20.650 --> 00:33:22.740
So. we can blow each other out of the sky...

673
00:33:22.740 --> 00:33:24.490
using what little power we have left...

674
00:33:24.780 --> 00:33:26.240
or we can try something different.

675
00:33:27.490 --> 00:33:29.080
We can explain ourselves to each other.

676
00:33:29.410 --> 00:33:31.080
<i>Understand each other. Empathize.</i>

677
00:33:31.660 --> 00:33:36.040
<i>If we don't. this war between us will simply continue. unabated.</i>

678
00:33:36.040 --> 00:33:37.540
<i>And the cost for that is sure.</i>

679
00:33:37.840 --> 00:33:38.960
Death.

680
00:33:39.710 --> 00:33:42.760
More and more death.

681
00:33:43.880 --> 00:33:46.340
Our peoples are indeed different. Captain.

682
00:33:47.090 --> 00:33:50.060
In our culture. your words are a show of weakness.

683
00:33:50.560 --> 00:33:54.100
<i>What chance does dialogue offer. save to delay me?</i>

684
00:33:54.100 --> 00:33:55.520
<i>Why should I listen to you?</i>

685
00:33:55.520 --> 00:33:56.890
PIKE: Both our ships are damaged.

686
00:33:56.900 --> 00:33:58.060
Your cloak is unstable...

687
00:33:58.060 --> 00:33:59.900
which leaves you vulnerable to our weapons.

688
00:33:59.900 --> 00:34:01.690
Maybe you have enough power to attack us.

689
00:34:01.690 --> 00:34:04.700
Maybe you have enough power to get back to Romulus without repairs.

690
00:34:05.070 --> 00:34:08.160
Conversely. maybe we can marshal our weapons and destroy you...

691
00:34:08.160 --> 00:34:09.740
before you make it to the Neutral Zone.

692
00:34:09.740 --> 00:34:12.040
<i>Or perhaps we chase you across the border...</i>

693
00:34:12.040 --> 00:34:14.410
<i>and destroy you and get out before anyone's the wiser.</i>

694
00:34:14.870 --> 00:34:17.000
So. what is it that you're suggesting. Captain?

695
00:34:17.790 --> 00:34:19.080
A good-faith gesture.

696
00:34:19.080 --> 00:34:20.210
2 hours.

697
00:34:20.500 --> 00:34:22.630
<i>Enough time to repair our ships and bury the dead.</i>

698
00:34:22.880 --> 00:34:24.340
<i>And maybe this bit of mercy...</i>

699
00:34:24.340 --> 00:34:27.340
will lead to something further and better...

700
00:34:27.340 --> 00:34:28.720
between our 2 cultures.

701
00:34:36.440 --> 00:34:37.520
[SIGHS SOFTLY]

702
00:34:41.730 --> 00:34:42.820
2 hours.

703
00:34:46.280 --> 00:34:47.610
[EXHALES]

704
00:34:49.490 --> 00:34:50.490
[SIGHS]

705
00:34:52.240 --> 00:34:53.580
Captain.

706
00:34:53.580 --> 00:34:54.790
They are lying.

707
00:34:55.160 --> 00:34:56.870
Romulans can't be trusted.

708
00:34:56.870 --> 00:34:58.580
They shot <i>Farragut</i> right in front of us.

709
00:34:58.580 --> 00:34:59.670
Stand down. Erica.

710
00:35:00.210 --> 00:35:01.580
You can't let them get away with it!

711
00:35:01.590 --> 00:35:02.920
Stand down!

712
00:35:06.920 --> 00:35:08.090
Yes. sir.

713
00:35:18.310 --> 00:35:19.480
Sensor readings suggest...

714
00:35:19.480 --> 00:35:21.230
the Romulans have stopped forward movement.

715
00:35:26.990 --> 00:35:28.780
I wonder what they're doing over there.

716
00:35:29.070 --> 00:35:30.280
Hopefully...

717
00:35:32.450 --> 00:35:33.780
same thing we are.

718
00:35:35.290 --> 00:35:36.540
SUBCOMMANDER: <i>A cease-fire?</i>

719
00:35:36.540 --> 00:35:39.000
This is Federation weakness.

720
00:35:39.460 --> 00:35:40.830
Is it not the Romulan way...

721
00:35:40.830 --> 00:35:42.880
to attack when we are given advantage like this?

722
00:35:42.880 --> 00:35:45.290
We are engaged in a cease-fire. SubCommander.

723
00:35:45.300 --> 00:35:46.800
We have 2 hours.

724
00:35:46.800 --> 00:35:48.510
Put all hands to repair our engines.

725
00:35:48.510 --> 00:35:50.880
If we do not. we will not make it back to Romulus.

726
00:35:50.880 --> 00:35:54.140
Sir. we should commit all hands to weapons repair.

727
00:35:54.560 --> 00:35:56.640
The Federation has given us the advantage.

728
00:35:56.970 --> 00:36:00.060
We can strike before this ridiculous cease-fire is completed.

729
00:36:07.820 --> 00:36:10.820
This is your 4ᵗʰ mission. is it not. SubCommander?

730
00:36:11.160 --> 00:36:13.030
3ʳᵈ. sir.

731
00:36:13.030 --> 00:36:15.910
I served with your uncle Tarqan during the Reman campaign.

732
00:36:15.910 --> 00:36:17.450
Did you know that. SubCommander?

733
00:36:17.450 --> 00:36:18.580
I did.

734
00:36:18.580 --> 00:36:21.160
His death was a great victory for Romulus.

735
00:36:21.170 --> 00:36:23.290
Yes. he was brave.

736
00:36:24.040 --> 00:36:26.340
His Commander. however. was a fool.

737
00:36:27.130 --> 00:36:29.340
He forced him to fight after we'd lost weapons...

738
00:36:29.340 --> 00:36:31.590
and the only logical choice was retreat.

739
00:36:31.590 --> 00:36:33.260
He did not have to die.

740
00:36:33.260 --> 00:36:34.680
Sir?

741
00:36:34.680 --> 00:36:36.050
His death was a waste.

742
00:36:36.560 --> 00:36:38.850
And it was stupid. It left us weaker.

743
00:36:39.520 --> 00:36:42.600
Now. I can say that because I'm old enough...

744
00:36:42.600 --> 00:36:44.690
and I don't care what people think of me.

745
00:36:45.270 --> 00:36:47.900
Pride is not something we can afford.

746
00:36:48.480 --> 00:36:51.360
We look at the world clearly on my ship.

747
00:36:51.360 --> 00:36:53.660
We do not make choices based on ego.

748
00:36:53.910 --> 00:36:55.530
Engines 1ˢᵗ.

749
00:36:55.530 --> 00:36:57.990
Then weapons. That is my order.

750
00:36:58.950 --> 00:37:00.290
Or are you so arrogant...

751
00:37:00.290 --> 00:37:02.210
you think you know better than your Commander?

752
00:37:03.540 --> 00:37:04.580
No. sir.

753
00:37:05.210 --> 00:37:06.380
Good.

754
00:37:06.880 --> 00:37:08.090
Because I need you.

755
00:37:08.090 --> 00:37:10.630
I don't know if this peace game...

756
00:37:10.630 --> 00:37:12.550
we're playing with the Federation will work.

757
00:37:12.550 --> 00:37:14.220
But I have to see it through.

758
00:37:14.220 --> 00:37:17.050
And if we achieve it. then good.

759
00:37:17.510 --> 00:37:18.510
But if not?

760
00:37:20.270 --> 00:37:22.020
Then you'll get your war.

761
00:37:35.410 --> 00:37:36.910
Do you want some coffee?

762
00:37:37.660 --> 00:37:40.410
I do not drink coffee. I do drink tea.

763
00:37:40.410 --> 00:37:42.250
All right. Would you like some tea?

764
00:37:42.250 --> 00:37:43.710
No. thank you. Captain.

765
00:37:45.420 --> 00:37:46.750
[CHUCKLING]

766
00:37:48.000 --> 00:37:50.320
Well. the more things change. the more they stay the same.

767
00:37:51.340 --> 00:37:53.130
It's good to see you're still you. Spock.

768
00:37:55.930 --> 00:37:57.550
So many things have gone wrong today.

769
00:37:59.100 --> 00:38:00.300
[SIGHS]

770
00:38:00.310 --> 00:38:03.310
The loss of Outpost 4. The destruction of the <i>Farragut.</i>

771
00:38:04.600 --> 00:38:07.060
Any one of them could set us on the path to a dark future.

772
00:38:08.770 --> 00:38:10.520
But I can't help feeling...

773
00:38:12.570 --> 00:38:14.190
there's something worse to come.

774
00:38:14.650 --> 00:38:18.280
Typically. no one can know the future in the moment.

775
00:38:18.950 --> 00:38:21.740
One can only follow one's instincts...

776
00:38:21.740 --> 00:38:23.500
and hope the truth will present itself.

777
00:38:24.620 --> 00:38:25.620
Spock...

778
00:38:27.000 --> 00:38:28.250
what happened to Una?

779
00:38:29.040 --> 00:38:32.170
She was sentenced to the Federation penal colony on Salius VI...

780
00:38:32.170 --> 00:38:34.210
where she has spent much of the last 7 years.

781
00:38:35.090 --> 00:38:36.130
Why?

782
00:38:36.510 --> 00:38:37.720
Her deception.

783
00:38:39.550 --> 00:38:40.970
I am confused.

784
00:38:40.970 --> 00:38:42.810
Even years ago. I thought you knew.

785
00:38:44.890 --> 00:38:47.060
[DOOR CHIMES]
- Come.

786
00:38:50.270 --> 00:38:52.270
SPOCK: If you'll excuse me. I wish to supervise...

787
00:38:52.270 --> 00:38:54.440
the repair of the phaser array personally.

788
00:38:58.030 --> 00:38:59.160
Captain.

789
00:39:00.070 --> 00:39:01.070
Captain.

790
00:39:04.580 --> 00:39:05.830
[DOOR WHOOSHES OPENS]

791
00:39:06.960 --> 00:39:09.170
I know you want me to change tack...

792
00:39:09.170 --> 00:39:11.290
but pride is just not something we can afford.

793
00:39:11.290 --> 00:39:13.000
You want me to tell you that I wouldn't have tried...

794
00:39:13.000 --> 00:39:15.010
to blow those Romulans out of the sky?

795
00:39:15.630 --> 00:39:16.970
Well. I would have.

796
00:39:18.090 --> 00:39:19.550
But it wasn't my call.

797
00:39:19.930 --> 00:39:21.760
Okay. We're here now.

798
00:39:21.760 --> 00:39:23.010
And the truth is...

799
00:39:24.180 --> 00:39:27.520
I don't know these Romulans can't be trusted.

800
00:39:28.440 --> 00:39:30.480
But I also don't know if they can.

801
00:39:30.730 --> 00:39:32.110
And neither do you.

802
00:39:33.400 --> 00:39:34.520
Fair enough.

803
00:39:36.690 --> 00:39:38.820
I'd like to explore a backup plan.

804
00:39:40.200 --> 00:39:42.870
If you'll give me the resources.

805
00:39:43.870 --> 00:39:45.030
I'm listening.

806
00:39:45.040 --> 00:39:47.620
Look. the Romulans just bought themselves some time.

807
00:39:47.620 --> 00:39:50.040
Sure. they can use that time to make repairs.

808
00:39:50.040 --> 00:39:53.500
But remember. they're on the edge of the Neutral Zone.

809
00:39:53.500 --> 00:39:55.800
They could also use it to call for reinforcements.

810
00:39:56.630 --> 00:39:59.130
So. what if we did the same?

811
00:39:59.380 --> 00:40:02.390
Just in case they decide to turn and fight after all.

812
00:40:03.220 --> 00:40:05.390
Jim. we're on the far edge of Federation space.

813
00:40:06.310 --> 00:40:08.310
It takes days to get a message to Starfleet.

814
00:40:08.310 --> 00:40:10.020
We're weeks away from help getting to us...

815
00:40:10.020 --> 00:40:11.350
even at maximum warp.

816
00:40:14.980 --> 00:40:17.110
But the Romulans don't know that.

817
00:40:19.780 --> 00:40:21.150
Captain Kirk...

818
00:40:22.860 --> 00:40:24.410
what are you suggesting?

819
00:40:25.410 --> 00:40:26.700
Captain Pike...

820
00:40:28.000 --> 00:40:29.750
can I borrow a shuttle?

821
00:40:46.510 --> 00:40:48.680
[SYSTEMS POWERING ON]

822
00:40:52.980 --> 00:40:54.310
Try it now.

823
00:40:54.310 --> 00:40:56.110
[ENGINEER IN SCOTTISH ACCENT] Aye. that's the one.

824
00:40:56.110 --> 00:40:58.440
This is where the auto repair was getting hung up.

825
00:40:58.440 --> 00:41:00.070
She's very fused.

826
00:41:00.070 --> 00:41:02.610
I do not need to remind you that we have less than 2 hours...

827
00:41:02.610 --> 00:41:04.490
to restore phaser control to working order.

828
00:41:04.490 --> 00:41:07.530
ENGINEER: I'm an engineer. not a miracle worker. Mr. Spock.

829
00:41:09.200 --> 00:41:10.620
2 minutes. Captain.

830
00:41:10.950 --> 00:41:12.160
Status?

831
00:41:12.160 --> 00:41:13.540
MITCHELL: We have engines...

832
00:41:13.540 --> 00:41:15.250
but weapons systems are not back online.

833
00:41:15.250 --> 00:41:17.080
Bridge to Spock. Status?

834
00:41:17.090 --> 00:41:18.290
SPOCK: <i>Working on it. Captain.</i>

835
00:41:18.300 --> 00:41:19.340
Working on it.

836
00:41:19.590 --> 00:41:20.880
UHURA: 2 hours. Captain.

837
00:41:21.300 --> 00:41:23.550
And... mark.

838
00:41:33.390 --> 00:41:35.150
Open a channel to the Romulan ship.

839
00:41:37.900 --> 00:41:39.650
Have you repaired your ship. Commander?

840
00:41:39.650 --> 00:41:41.650
Have you repaired yours. Captain?

841
00:41:43.030 --> 00:41:44.400
Conventional wisdom suggests...

842
00:41:44.400 --> 00:41:46.320
that our next move is to resume hostilities.

843
00:41:46.320 --> 00:41:47.660
To fight.

844
00:41:47.660 --> 00:41:49.370
<i>You yourself told me that in your culture...</i>

845
00:41:49.370 --> 00:41:51.370
<i>to do anything else would be a sign of weakness.</i>

846
00:41:51.700 --> 00:41:54.330
But let me tell you a way in which humans are not weak.

847
00:41:54.870 --> 00:41:57.330
Our strength comes from our willingness to see a partner...

848
00:41:57.330 --> 00:41:58.630
instead of an enemy.

849
00:41:58.630 --> 00:42:00.000
<i>In our culture. that is an act...</i>

850
00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:01.500
<i>of faith and strength...</i>

851
00:42:01.510 --> 00:42:03.170
<i>not a failure of character.</i>

852
00:42:03.880 --> 00:42:05.630
Do Romulans have that kind of strength?

853
00:42:12.680 --> 00:42:15.440
I. too. tire of endless war.

854
00:42:22.940 --> 00:42:24.950
[INTERMITTENT BEEPING]

855
00:42:25.400 --> 00:42:27.410
[ALARM BLARING]

856
00:42:46.930 --> 00:42:48.760
Why is the fleet here? I did not call for them.

857
00:42:48.760 --> 00:42:50.890
I alerted them of our situation. Commander.

858
00:42:51.390 --> 00:42:53.010
The Federation showed weakness.

859
00:42:53.720 --> 00:42:55.600
It is the Romulan way to strike.

860
00:42:55.890 --> 00:42:57.640
You were not going to.

861
00:42:57.640 --> 00:42:59.400
I took matters into my own hands.

862
00:42:59.400 --> 00:43:02.060
You disobeyed a direct order.

863
00:43:02.070 --> 00:43:03.980
Had you not negotiated with the Federation...

864
00:43:03.980 --> 00:43:05.320
I would not have needed to.

865
00:43:05.320 --> 00:43:08.570
We undertook this mission to test the strength of the Federation.

866
00:43:09.110 --> 00:43:10.820
They showed us they lack it.

867
00:43:10.820 --> 00:43:13.080
We should have destroyed them the moment they did.

868
00:43:13.080 --> 00:43:15.620
You don't remember a time without war.

869
00:43:16.200 --> 00:43:17.580
But I do.

870
00:43:18.370 --> 00:43:20.420
Who wins an endless war with the Federation?

871
00:43:20.420 --> 00:43:22.250
We will. Commander.

872
00:43:22.250 --> 00:43:25.630
An endless war. by definition. can never be won.

873
00:43:26.840 --> 00:43:28.630
Captain Pike will not trust my word now.

874
00:43:28.630 --> 00:43:30.300
What does that matter?

875
00:43:31.340 --> 00:43:32.760
He will be dead soon.

876
00:43:32.760 --> 00:43:33.930
[SCOFFS]

877
00:43:35.020 --> 00:43:36.390
Take him off the bridge.

878
00:43:51.410 --> 00:43:52.950
UHURA: We're being hailed. sir.

879
00:43:52.950 --> 00:43:54.450
It's the Romulan flagship.

880
00:43:54.450 --> 00:43:55.700
On screen.

881
00:43:57.830 --> 00:43:59.370
<i>Human.</i>

882
00:43:59.370 --> 00:44:01.960
<i>I am here to accept your unconditional surrender.</i>

883
00:44:02.380 --> 00:44:03.960
Nice to meet you too.

884
00:44:03.960 --> 00:44:06.380
I'm Captain Pike of the Federation Starship <i>Enterprise.</i>

885
00:44:06.380 --> 00:44:07.460
And you are?

886
00:44:07.460 --> 00:44:09.420
You may address me as Praetor.

887
00:44:09.420 --> 00:44:10.930
It is customary to kneel.

888
00:44:10.930 --> 00:44:13.470
As I'm not a Romulan. you'll forgive me if I don't.

889
00:44:13.470 --> 00:44:15.050
Now. I'm confused.

890
00:44:15.060 --> 00:44:17.810
We are holding to our side of the Neutral Zone. as you are.

891
00:44:18.390 --> 00:44:19.850
Yet you demand our surrender?

892
00:44:19.850 --> 00:44:22.310
Captain. I have you surrounded.

893
00:44:22.310 --> 00:44:24.480
Surrender or we will destroy you.

894
00:44:24.900 --> 00:44:26.650
You have 1 minute to comply.

895
00:44:26.650 --> 00:44:27.650
[COMM CHANNEL CLOSES]

896
00:44:28.360 --> 00:44:29.740
You know. I don't like her.

897
00:44:29.990 --> 00:44:31.320
Perimeter alert.

898
00:44:31.320 --> 00:44:33.490
We have ships incoming. sir. Dozens.

899
00:44:33.490 --> 00:44:35.200
More Romulans?
- No.

900
00:44:35.200 --> 00:44:37.450
They look like ours.

901
00:44:52.010 --> 00:44:54.010
I've got a secure channel from the lead ship. sir.

902
00:44:54.640 --> 00:44:55.680
It's Captain Kirk.

903
00:44:57.680 --> 00:45:00.020
<i>Chris. the reinforcements you ordered?</i>

904
00:45:00.850 --> 00:45:04.400
<i>Been 100 years since the Federation has seen the Romulans.</i>

905
00:45:04.400 --> 00:45:06.230
We didn't know what their ships looked like...

906
00:45:06.230 --> 00:45:08.940
and so I figured they don't know what ours look like either.

907
00:45:09.190 --> 00:45:11.570
All robotic mining craft?

908
00:45:11.570 --> 00:45:14.410
Mining. hauling. Not one of them manned.

909
00:45:14.410 --> 00:45:15.700
But to the Romulans...

910
00:45:15.700 --> 00:45:19.080
who's to say we aren't a Federation armada?

911
00:45:19.870 --> 00:45:21.540
You sneaky son of a bitch.

912
00:45:21.540 --> 00:45:23.710
It's enough to bluff with. I hope.

913
00:45:24.370 --> 00:45:25.960
Try not to get us in a real fight.

914
00:45:25.960 --> 00:45:28.550
I'll do my best. Thanks. Captain.

915
00:45:29.590 --> 00:45:31.050
It's my pleasure. Captain.

916
00:45:31.340 --> 00:45:32.550
Bridge to Spock.

917
00:45:32.550 --> 00:45:34.720
We really could use some phasers right about now.

918
00:45:34.720 --> 00:45:36.970
<i>How's it going down there?</i>
- We are making progress.

919
00:45:36.970 --> 00:45:38.850
The conduits are severely damaged.

920
00:45:38.850 --> 00:45:40.060
PIKE: Work faster. Mr. Spock.

921
00:45:40.060 --> 00:45:41.220
We're going to need weapons soon...

922
00:45:41.220 --> 00:45:42.640
or we're not going to need them at all.

923
00:45:42.640 --> 00:45:44.180
The Romulan Praetor is hailing us. sir.

924
00:45:44.190 --> 00:45:46.750
Keep a secure channel open for Captain Kirk so he can listen in.

925
00:45:50.030 --> 00:45:51.150
You ready to sell this?

926
00:45:52.110 --> 00:45:53.650
Ready as I'll ever be.

927
00:45:58.580 --> 00:46:00.410
By now you've probably noticed...

928
00:46:00.410 --> 00:46:03.540
our armada of Starfleet Delta-class attack ships.

929
00:46:04.080 --> 00:46:06.920
But we won't have to use them. will we. Praetor?

930
00:46:06.920 --> 00:46:08.830
This is an act of unparalleled aggression...

931
00:46:08.840 --> 00:46:10.800
on the border of our territory. Captain.

932
00:46:11.130 --> 00:46:12.920
No. just a standard training maneuver...

933
00:46:12.920 --> 00:46:15.320
that happened to land our fleet here the same time as yours.

934
00:46:15.760 --> 00:46:19.300
You want to know what actually is an act of unparalleled aggression?

935
00:46:19.890 --> 00:46:22.930
A Romulan bird-of-prey using cloaking technology...

936
00:46:22.930 --> 00:46:25.020
destroying our Neutral Zone outposts.

937
00:46:25.020 --> 00:46:26.730
I know nothing of what you speak.

938
00:46:26.730 --> 00:46:29.060
That's okay. We'll send you a recording of it decloaking...

939
00:46:29.060 --> 00:46:30.730
right before destroying Outpost 4.

940
00:46:35.400 --> 00:46:37.070
[EXPLOSION ON RECORDING]

941
00:46:40.330 --> 00:46:41.450
PRAETOR: <i>I see.</i>

942
00:46:43.410 --> 00:46:45.410
[WHIRRING]
- [COMMS CHIMING]

943
00:46:45.410 --> 00:46:48.290
Romulan ship is decloaking and breaking formation.

944
00:46:48.290 --> 00:46:49.670
Heading our way.

945
00:46:49.670 --> 00:46:51.000
Praetor. what is this?

946
00:46:51.000 --> 00:46:52.380
This is a culling. Captain.

947
00:46:52.380 --> 00:46:55.590
<i>That Commander should not have allowed himself to be caught.</i>

948
00:46:56.380 --> 00:46:57.590
ORTEGAS: Sir.

949
00:46:58.180 --> 00:46:59.930
It's the bird-of-prey we've been chasing.

950
00:46:59.930 --> 00:47:01.810
Nyota. pause communication.

951
00:47:02.680 --> 00:47:04.430
Open a channel with the Romulan Commander.

952
00:47:05.480 --> 00:47:06.640
[COMMS CHIMING]

953
00:47:06.640 --> 00:47:07.810
Captain.

954
00:47:11.310 --> 00:47:13.980
So. we see each other once again. after all.

955
00:47:14.230 --> 00:47:15.320
What are you doing?

956
00:47:15.320 --> 00:47:16.650
<i>Only what is asked of me.</i>

957
00:47:17.400 --> 00:47:18.820
I never called for that armada.

958
00:47:18.820 --> 00:47:20.410
We can beam you and your crew aboard.

959
00:47:20.410 --> 00:47:21.660
You don't have to do this.

960
00:47:21.660 --> 00:47:23.080
It is not our way.

961
00:47:24.120 --> 00:47:25.870
I regret that we meet in this way.

962
00:47:26.620 --> 00:47:28.000
You and I are of a kind.

963
00:47:28.710 --> 00:47:31.540
In a different reality. I could've called you friend.

964
00:47:32.130 --> 00:47:34.170
What purpose will it serve to die?

965
00:47:34.170 --> 00:47:36.420
We are creatures of duty. you and I.

966
00:47:37.630 --> 00:47:39.590
Just 1 more duty to perform.

967
00:47:40.340 --> 00:47:43.850
Do not be upset. I have accepted my fate.

968
00:47:45.010 --> 00:47:47.140
Perhaps someday. my sacrifice will lead...

969
00:47:47.140 --> 00:47:49.100
to an end to this conflict between us.

970
00:48:07.330 --> 00:48:08.710
They're powering up weapons.

971
00:48:28.390 --> 00:48:30.350
[SYSTEM CHIMING]

972
00:48:30.350 --> 00:48:32.940
The Romulan Praetor is hailing us again. sir.

973
00:48:44.620 --> 00:48:45.870
On screen.

974
00:48:47.620 --> 00:48:49.290
<i>Our fleet is stronger now.</i>

975
00:48:49.290 --> 00:48:51.540
<i>And I am ready to accept your surrender.</i>

976
00:48:51.540 --> 00:48:54.000
This is really how you want to end 100 years of peace?

977
00:48:54.000 --> 00:48:55.790
What do Romulans care of peace?

978
00:48:55.790 --> 00:48:57.380
It means nothing to us.

979
00:48:57.380 --> 00:49:00.090
<i>And your apparent affinity for it has sealed your fate.</i>

980
00:49:00.090 --> 00:49:01.470
<i>Thank you. Captain Pike.</i>

981
00:49:01.470 --> 00:49:03.930
If not for your weakness. we would have never known...

982
00:49:03.930 --> 00:49:06.600
what easy targets your Federation would be.

983
00:49:07.220 --> 00:49:08.390
<i>Goodbye.</i>

984
00:49:09.890 --> 00:49:11.270
They're powering up weapons again.

985
00:49:11.270 --> 00:49:13.480
Evasive maneuvers. Erica. Pattern Zeta-3.

986
00:49:21.110 --> 00:49:22.690
Kirk. get back here. We're about to warp out.

987
00:49:22.700 --> 00:49:23.780
Roger that.

988
00:49:23.780 --> 00:49:25.700
Captain. warp engines aren't engaging.

989
00:49:26.450 --> 00:49:27.490
Erica.

990
00:49:28.030 --> 00:49:29.410
I'm sorry. sir.

991
00:49:29.410 --> 00:49:30.950
MITCHELL: Sir. the drone ships are moving.

992
00:49:30.950 --> 00:49:32.410
Son of a bitch.

993
00:49:32.410 --> 00:49:33.660
Kirk. what are you doing?

994
00:49:33.670 --> 00:49:35.960
Covering your escape. Get those engines fixed.

995
00:49:41.970 --> 00:49:44.410
ORTEGAS: He's putting the drones between us and the Romulans.

996
00:49:53.140 --> 00:49:54.810
[GRUNTING]

997
00:50:00.020 --> 00:50:01.480
MITCHELL: Captain Kirk has beamed on board.

998
00:50:01.480 --> 00:50:02.900
Engines online. Captain.

999
00:50:04.280 --> 00:50:05.280
Hit it.

1000
00:50:06.200 --> 00:50:07.870
[ENGINES POWERING UP]

1001
00:50:11.370 --> 00:50:12.370
[SIGHS]

1002
00:50:13.870 --> 00:50:15.330
Damage report.

1003
00:50:15.330 --> 00:50:17.120
MITCHELL: Reports coming from all decks.

1004
00:50:17.130 --> 00:50:18.420
Captain.

1005
00:50:18.420 --> 00:50:21.840
The Romulans are broadcasting on all known subspace frequencies.

1006
00:50:24.130 --> 00:50:26.010
It's a declaration of war. sir.

1007
00:50:27.010 --> 00:50:28.390
Against the Federation.

1008
00:50:33.930 --> 00:50:37.480
MITCHELL: Decks 5. 11. 12 & 22 are all reporting hull breaches.

1009
00:50:37.480 --> 00:50:39.440
Weapons systems took a direct hit.

1010
00:50:39.690 --> 00:50:40.900
Spock.

1011
00:50:44.190 --> 00:50:45.240
Medical.

1012
00:51:04.430 --> 00:51:07.200
♪♪

1013
00:51:30.330 --> 00:51:33.100
♪♪

1014
00:51:56.640 --> 00:51:58.430
Massive cerebral trauma.

1015
00:51:58.890 --> 00:52:00.230
Major blood loss.

1016
00:52:01.980 --> 00:52:03.360
Spinal fractures.

1017
00:52:04.610 --> 00:52:06.030
Radiation burns across...

1018
00:52:07.030 --> 00:52:08.610
40% of his body.

1019
00:52:14.990 --> 00:52:17.290
I'm not sure that he will recover from this.

1020
00:52:20.540 --> 00:52:21.790
But if he does...

1021
00:52:23.210 --> 00:52:24.420
he will not be the same.

1022
00:52:59.500 --> 00:53:01.140
FUTURE PIKE: I know what you're thinking.

1023
00:53:04.500 --> 00:53:06.880
I was thinking the same thing when I went through this.

1024
00:53:09.630 --> 00:53:11.510
That I traded my fate for Spock's?

1025
00:53:11.510 --> 00:53:12.550
Yes.

1026
00:53:13.220 --> 00:53:14.970
This isn't going to help...

1027
00:53:16.890 --> 00:53:18.140
but it gets worse.

1028
00:53:19.390 --> 00:53:21.100
This war with the Romulans.

1029
00:53:22.020 --> 00:53:23.230
Millions die.

1030
00:53:24.020 --> 00:53:25.770
So far. It's still going on.

1031
00:53:26.520 --> 00:53:30.190
Not only did you start something that should never have been started.

1032
00:53:30.860 --> 00:53:32.530
The best chance at a lasting peace...

1033
00:53:32.530 --> 00:53:35.070
between the Federation and the Romulans in any timeline?

1034
00:53:36.530 --> 00:53:37.580
Well...

1035
00:53:37.950 --> 00:53:40.040
turns out he's lying in a biobed.

1036
00:53:41.870 --> 00:53:44.160
We all want to think our future is important.

1037
00:53:44.170 --> 00:53:46.380
And ours. yours and mine. it is.

1038
00:53:47.790 --> 00:53:49.210
Just not the way you think.

1039
00:53:49.960 --> 00:53:51.130
Time is. uh...

1040
00:53:52.260 --> 00:53:53.550
It's complicated.

1041
00:53:55.470 --> 00:53:57.550
But the monks showed me something simple.

1042
00:53:58.180 --> 00:54:02.350
Every time we change the path...

1043
00:54:02.350 --> 00:54:03.560
he dies.

1044
00:54:05.060 --> 00:54:06.650
And he's got things to do.

1045
00:54:10.900 --> 00:54:12.610
Fate-of-the-galaxy-type things.

1046
00:54:14.030 --> 00:54:15.400
Paths diverge.

1047
00:54:17.370 --> 00:54:20.540
But I am the result of one that should never have been taken.

1048
00:54:23.410 --> 00:54:24.830
Thank you.
- Hey...

1049
00:54:24.830 --> 00:54:26.250
look at it this way.

1050
00:54:27.250 --> 00:54:29.040
How many people get to give their life for someone...

1051
00:54:29.040 --> 00:54:30.250
twice in 1 day?

1052
00:54:31.250 --> 00:54:33.510
See? Twice. 'cause there's 2 of us and we're both...

1053
00:54:33.510 --> 00:54:34.630
Yeah. I... I got it.

1054
00:54:35.680 --> 00:54:36.680
Got it.

1055
00:54:40.930 --> 00:54:42.100
[DOOR CHIMES]

1056
00:54:43.060 --> 00:54:44.430
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

1057
00:54:44.430 --> 00:54:45.560
Oh. yeah.

1058
00:54:51.270 --> 00:54:52.360
Come.

1059
00:54:53.860 --> 00:54:55.360
Not interrupting. am I?

1060
00:54:57.110 --> 00:54:58.570
No. I...

1061
00:54:58.570 --> 00:55:00.120
[DOOR WHOOSHES SHUT]

1062
00:55:00.120 --> 00:55:01.490
Not really. I'm just. uh...

1063
00:55:03.240 --> 00:55:04.700
talking to myself.

1064
00:55:06.790 --> 00:55:08.080
Fancy a drink?

1065
00:55:08.540 --> 00:55:09.630
Sure.

1066
00:55:12.460 --> 00:55:13.800
You know. uh...

1067
00:55:16.720 --> 00:55:18.300
I don't think I can explain it...

1068
00:55:21.510 --> 00:55:23.510
but I think I was supposed to meet you.

1069
00:55:25.520 --> 00:55:27.390
I get that feeling too.

1070
00:55:28.640 --> 00:55:31.610
I. uh. honestly just came by to check on you.

1071
00:55:32.270 --> 00:55:34.940
I'm sorry things went down the way they did.

1072
00:55:36.240 --> 00:55:37.820
You tried for something better.

1073
00:55:40.070 --> 00:55:41.240
Tried and lost.

1074
00:55:42.370 --> 00:55:43.370
[GLASSES CLINK]

1075
00:55:48.620 --> 00:55:51.250
Did it ever occur to you that sometimes...

1076
00:55:51.250 --> 00:55:53.210
you can't avoid a fight?

1077
00:55:53.210 --> 00:55:55.210
If you had just chased that Romulan ship...

1078
00:55:55.210 --> 00:55:57.090
from the get-go and taken it out...

1079
00:55:57.380 --> 00:55:59.260
maybe none of this would've happened.

1080
00:56:01.180 --> 00:56:02.850
You're a good Captain. Jim Kirk.

1081
00:56:05.680 --> 00:56:07.480
<i>Enterprise</i> would be lucky to have you.

1082
00:56:08.390 --> 00:56:09.890
You thinking of retiring?

1083
00:56:09.890 --> 00:56:11.100
[CHUCKLING] No.

1084
00:56:11.560 --> 00:56:13.810
Oh. no. No. not yet.

1085
00:56:15.940 --> 00:56:17.150
So...

1086
00:56:17.780 --> 00:56:19.860
come on over and have a seat. Captain.

1087
00:56:22.910 --> 00:56:24.280
Tell me about yourself.

1088
00:56:26.870 --> 00:56:28.250
Where are you from?

1089
00:56:29.040 --> 00:56:32.120
[SIGHS] I grew up in Iowa.

1090
00:56:32.120 --> 00:56:34.880
[FADING] My father. George. was the 1ˢᵗ Officer on the <i>Kelvin</i>...

1091
00:56:34.880 --> 00:56:36.670
before he moved to <i>Charleston...</i>

1092
00:57:07.910 --> 00:57:09.870
Computer...
- [COMPUTER CHIMES]

1093
00:57:09.870 --> 00:57:11.250
Delete file.

1094
00:57:31.020 --> 00:57:32.100
[DOOR CHIMES]

1095
00:57:32.100 --> 00:57:33.180
PIKE: Come.

1096
00:57:33.190 --> 00:57:34.520
[DOOR WHOOSHES OPEN]

1097
00:57:35.400 --> 00:57:36.900
SPOCK: Captain.

1098
00:57:36.900 --> 00:57:38.860
Am I interrupting?
- No.

1099
00:57:40.820 --> 00:57:42.280
I'm very glad to see you.

1100
00:57:44.110 --> 00:57:45.700
But you saw me only moments ago.

1101
00:57:46.530 --> 00:57:47.660
Right.

1102
00:57:47.660 --> 00:57:49.120
You left the briefing suddenly.

1103
00:57:49.790 --> 00:57:52.250
It was uncharacteristic.

1104
00:57:53.160 --> 00:57:54.330
Was it?

1105
00:57:56.130 --> 00:57:58.590
But now your demeanor appears changed.

1106
00:57:59.840 --> 00:58:01.420
Having heard the boy's name...

1107
00:58:01.420 --> 00:58:03.970
I cannot help but wonder if this pertains to your future.

1108
00:58:06.300 --> 00:58:07.720
Let's just say...

1109
00:58:08.600 --> 00:58:11.560
I think the universe is telling me that some fates are inescapable.

1110
00:58:13.100 --> 00:58:14.770
And even if I could get out of mine...

1111
00:58:15.940 --> 00:58:17.650
it might just fall to someone else.

1112
00:58:18.810 --> 00:58:20.320
Someone you know?

1113
00:58:20.320 --> 00:58:21.480
Yes.

1114
00:58:22.690 --> 00:58:24.950
Is that why you are very glad to see me?

1115
00:58:30.740 --> 00:58:33.450
I believe I may owe you a debt of gratitude. Captain.

1116
00:58:33.450 --> 00:58:36.330
Although for precisely what. I do not know.

1117
00:58:36.830 --> 00:58:38.670
Spock. you are...

1118
00:58:42.550 --> 00:58:44.130
You are very important to me.

1119
00:58:44.130 --> 00:58:45.470
As are you to me. Captain.

1120
00:58:47.340 --> 00:58:48.510
Chris.

1121
00:58:56.390 --> 00:58:58.770
[ ♪ MELISSA CARPER - "MAKIN' MEMORIES" ♪ ]

1122
00:58:58.770 --> 00:58:59.850
[DOOR WHOOSHES SHUT]

